  - Include #44's exact starter list as a row.\n4. **Expose a pure selection function** so #45 and #44 can test the starter config without the worker harness. Add `func (r *Resolved) SelectReviewers(worker Role, changed []string, triageRan func(string) bool) []string` in `internal/config`. It returns the base set only, in config order. `(*job).reviewers` calls it, then appends the deferred and `next` reviewers. Table-test it in `internal/config`.\n5. **Worker `reviewers:` list.** Unless the owner rules otherwise (Q1), the list narrows the candidate set and each candidate's `when:` still applies. It does not bypass `when:`. Reason: under bypass, `reviewers: [eng-review, license-review]` would run license-review on every PR, so a worker could not restrict its reviewers without losing their gating. Lead-deferred reviewers (`closeout.Deferred`) and the worker role file's own `next` review requests (added in `buildWorker`) always bypass `when:`. Test both.\n6. **Changed-path range (bug).** `localRef(jb.branch)` (`refs/ard/<branch>`) exists only for a branch that was fetched at the start of the job. On a new branch it does not exist, and after this job's push it is stale.\n   - Record the pushed head in `push()` (`jb.head = res.SHA`). Use `s.h.BaseSHA` for the no-code path in `round`.\n   - Compute changed paths as `ChangedPaths(RepoDir, MergeBase(RepoDir, jb.cfg.SHA, head), head)`. `MergeBase` is already on the worker `Git` interface.\n   - `finishWithPR` reaches `openPR` too, so use `jb.head` there as well.\n   - If `head` is empty or all zeros (a dry-run `CommitCode` returns a synthetic zero SHA), skip git and fail open without a warning.\n7. **Renames and deletions.** `git diff --name-only` uses rename detection by default (`diff.renames`), so a rename lists only the new path. A move out of `web/` would then miss a `web/` rule. Add `--no-renames` to `gitx.ChangedPaths`, so a rename lists both old and new paths. This only makes the committer's declared-path check stricter. Add a gitx test (rename lists both paths, a deletion is listed), and run the committer tests. Deleted paths count as changed.\n8. **Exclude all of `.ard/`, not just `excluded()`.** The reviewer's `diff.patch` excludes `:(top,exclude).ard/`, and the diff guard bars any other `.ard/` path on a worker branch. Drop every path under `.ard/` (and `.ard-input/`) before matching, so a reviewer is never selected by a close-out file. Note in the docs that `when.paths` cannot select on `.ard/`.\n9. **\"A triage role ran.\"** A role counts as having run when either source shows it:\n   - a closed, done triage close-out in state (the plan's `closeout.TriageRoles`), or\n   - the issue carries `ard:triage:<role>:done`, read from `jb.is.Labels` through `labels.Done`.\n\n   The union keeps the rule working after `ard rebuild-state` and matches the #45 test plan, which uses the label. A needs-human or failed triage does not count (Q2). If the store read errors, fall back to the labels alone and log `worker.reviewers_failed`.\n10. **Selection is monotonic across pushes.** Every worker run (a re-claim, or a #41 fix round) recomputes the set from the whole PR diff (merge base to head). Close-out only adds request labels and never removes one, so a reviewer requested earlier stays requested even when later commits no longer match. A reviewer that starts to match on a later push is added. Put this sentence in the proposal and the `reviewers` doc comment. Add a worker test: run 1 does not touch `go.mod`, so license-review is not requested; run 2 on the same branch adds `go.mod`, so it is requested; eng-review is not duplicated.\n11. **Empty selection.** If reviewer roles exist but none is selected, log `worker.no_reviewers` at Warn with the issue and PR. Do not change gates. `prgate.Labels` returns `ReasonNoReviews` and `maybeReady` leaves the PR a draft for a human. Say so in the proposal.\n12. **Fail open, precisely.** When git fails, every role whose `Paths` is non-empty is treated as matched; triage still uses whatever it could read. Log one `worker.reviewers_failed` with a `step` attribute (`merge_base`, `changed_paths` or `triage`). Add tests for a git error and a store error.\n13. **Docs.**\n    - `docs/proposal.md` step 8 (line ~305): drop \"`when:` rules are ignored until #42\" and state the rules from 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 11.\n    - The Reviewer loop paragraph (line ~339) and the Configuration example (line ~400): the root-only `package*.json` becomes `**/package*.json`, `go.mod` becomes `**/go.mod`, and so on. Add one `web/` prefix example.\n    - The doc comment on `config.When`: replace \"Semantics are owned by #15\" with a pointer to `Matches`.\n    - `internal/roles/config.yaml` comments, if any mention `when:`.\n14. **Tests to add** beyond the plan: amendments 1, 2, 3, 5, 6 (a new branch, where `refs/ard/` is absent), 7, 9 (label only, state only), 10, 11 and 12. Also a test that `Matches` is never consulted when the tests failed (`buildWorker` already skips requests then).\n\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-23T15:21:58Z\n\n<!-- ard:triage regate body=49101a2bab03 -->\n**ard · triage · paused**\n\nThe title or body of this issue changed after it was admitted for triage, so ard stopped. A maintainer can review the change, re-apply `ard:pending` and remove `ard:needs-human` to continue.\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-23T15:23:24Z\n\n<!-- ard:closeout job=01M84G1520K1EB1WET8A0DR14X attempt=1 -->\n**ard · triage:engineer · done**\n\nReplaces the earlier plan with one that evaluates reviewer when: rules at PR time, using the owner's amendments: directory-rule normalisation, a correct merge-base diff range, rename handling, a pure selection function, and a config check warning. Size L, risk medium because it decides which reviews gate a PR.\n\n## Open issues\n- The plan touches `internal/roles/config.yaml` only if it mentions when:; if that file is protected or needs a human edit, a maintainer should do it.\n- Needs a look that the committer's declared-path check is acceptable with the stricter rename listing.\n\nOutput: [.ard/42/triage-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/12de0dc91396f2f264d7dbbd15ecec3359043db4/.ard/42/triage-engineer.md) · log [.ard/42/logs/triage-engineer-20261123T152243.913Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/12de0dc91396f2f264d7dbbd15ecec3359043db4/.ard/42/logs/triage-engineer-20261123T152243.913Z.log) · job `01M84G1520K1EB1WET8A0DR14X` · attempt 1\n\n\n### ard-bot-albertcbrown[bot] at 2026-11-23T15:29:05Z\n\n<!-- ard:triage gate=approval job=01M84E8EKM9Z61D1YTWJWRPAAX -->\n**ard · triage · ready for approval**\n\nTriage is complete; the plan is in `.ard/42/plan.md`. A maintainer adds `ard:approved` to start the `engineer` worker. An approval given before triage finished does not count: remove and re-add the label.\n\n# Plan for #42\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\n\nCurrent state: `(*job).reviewers` in `internal/worker/run.go` takes `jb.role.Reviewers` or every reviewer role, then appends `closeout.Deferred` review requests. `config.When{Paths, Triage}` (`internal/config/types.go`) is parsed and validated in `applyOverride` (`internal/config/load.go`) but never evaluated. Matching helper `matchProtected` and `normaliseProtectedPath` live in `internal/config/protected.go`. The owner's amendments (issue body) are folded in below.\n\n1. `internal/config/load.go`, `applyOverride` (when block): (a) normalise each `when.paths` entry with `normaliseProtectedPath`, not `normaliseRelPath`, so a trailing `/` survives, globs are validated, keep the `%s.when.paths[%d]` error key; (b) reject a non-nil rule with no paths and no triage: \"when must set paths or triage; remove when: to run on every PR\" (`when: null` stays \"always\"). Check `render.go` output and the `go.mod,package*.json` assertion in `load_test.go` still hold.\n2. `internal/config/types.go`: replace \"Semantics are owned by #15\" on `When` with a pointer to `Matches`. Add `func (w *When) Matches(changed []string, triageRan func(role string) bool) bool`: nil matches; else (any changed path matches any `Paths` entry via `matchProtected`) OR (any `Triage` role has `triageRan` true). Doc comment pins: case-sensitive, anchored at repo root; entry ending `/` is a directory on a segment boundary; otherwise doublestar glob (`*` within a segment, `**` crosses, `**/go.mod` matches root `go.mod`); slash-free glob matches only at root.\n3. `internal/config` (new file `select.go`): `func (r *Resolved) SelectReviewers(worker Role, changed []string, triageRan func(string) bool) []string`. Candidates are `worker.Reviewers` when non-empty (only existing reviewer roles), else every reviewer role, in config order; keep a candidate whose `When.Matches` is true. Returns the base set only. A worker `reviewers:` list narrows candidates and never bypasses `when:`.\n4. `internal/gitx/local.go`, `ChangedPaths`: add `--no-renames` to the diff args so a rename lists old and new paths and deletions are listed. Update the doc comment. Run committer tests (the declared-path check becomes stricter).\n5. `internal/closeout/closeout.go` (new): `func TriageRoles(ctx, s, issue int) (map[string]bool, error)` modelled on `Deferred`: `CloseoutsOf(ctx, issue, StageTriage)`, keep `Phase == PhaseClosed` and `Plan.Outcome == OutcomeDone` (needs-human and failed excluded), return the set of `Job.Role`.\n6. `internal/worker/loop.go`: add `ChangedPaths(ctx, dir, from, to string, paths ...string) ([]string, error)` to the `Git` interface (`*gitx.Git` already has it); update the fake in `internal/worker/harness_test.go`.\n7. `internal/worker/run.go`:\n   - Add `head string` to `job`. In `push()` set `jb.head = res.SHA`; in `round`'s no-code path use `s.h.BaseSHA`. `finishWithPR` reaches `openPR`, so it uses `jb.head` as well.\n   - Rewrite `reviewers` doc comment (state monotonic selection: each run recomputes from the whole PR diff, close-out only adds labels, so earlier requests stay and newly matching reviewers are added) and body:\n     - `head` empty or all zeros: skip git, fail open (every role with non-empty `Paths` matched), no warning.\n     - Otherwise `base, err := MergeBase(RepoDir, jb.cfg.SHA, head)`, then `ChangedPaths(RepoDir, base, head)`. On error log one `worker.reviewers_failed` with `step` = `merge_base` or `changed_paths` and fail open for path rules.\n     - Drop every path under `.ard/` and `.ard-input/` before matching.\n     - `triageRan` = union of `closeout.TriageRoles` and `labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, role)` present in `jb.is.Labels`. On store error log `worker.reviewers_failed` `step=triage` and use labels alone.\n     - Call `jb.cfg.SelectReviewers(jb.role, changed, triageRan)`, then append lead `closeout.Deferred` review requests and the worker role file's own `next` review requests (added in `buildWorker`) unconditionally; keep existence check, de-dup, stable order.\n     - If reviewer roles exist and the final set is empty, log `worker.no_reviewers` at Warn with issue and PR. Gates are unchanged (`prgate` returns `ReasonNoReviews`, PR stays draft).\n   - Tests failing already skips requests in `buildWorker`; do not evaluate `Matches` then.\n8. `internal/configcmd/config.go`, `Check`: when reviewer roles exist and every one has a `When`, print a warning to `e.Stderr` (not an error, exit code unchanged) that a PR matching none stays a draft.\n9. Docs: `docs/proposal.md` step 8 (~line 305): drop \"`when:` rules are ignored until #42\" and state paths OR triage, worker list narrows, `next` bypasses, changed-path range (merge base to head), `.ard/` not selectable, `done`-only triage, monotonic selection, empty selection leaves a draft, fail-open. Reviewer loop (~339) and Configuration example (~400): `**/package*.json`, `**/go.mod`, add a `web/` example; document the `config check` warning. Update `internal/roles/config.yaml` comments if they mention `when:`.\n\n### Test plan\n\nRun `go test ./intern