{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012ihjpYnd4HjuVAGBzn8UX1","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/proposal.md:171:{\"fingerprint\":\"osv:GHSA-xxxx:go.mod:golang.org/x/net\",\"title\":\"golang.org/x/net: GHSA-xxxx (high)\",\ndocs/proposal.md:172: \"severity\":\"high\",\"group\":\"go.mod\",\"files\":[\"go.mod\"],\"body\":\"markdown details\"}\ndocs/proposal.md:203:| lts | endoflife.date + manifests: go.mod, package.json, Dockerfile `FROM`, Helm charts | 7 d | 1 per component | yes |\ndocs/proposal.md:305:8. **Open or update a draft PR** with ard's own `Closes #<issue>`, the agent summary quoted and neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`, then marker and mention defusing), the test result and links to `worker-<role>.md`, the logs and the job id. Reviewers are the role's `reviewers`, or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty (`when:` rules are ignored until #42), plus any `review:<role>` the lead deferred, limited to roles that exist, and requested only when the tests did not fail. The PR stays a draft; the merger marks it ready. A job that has pushed always gets its draft PR, even when it then ends in `ard:needs-human` or a failure, so pushed work is never left without one.\ndocs/proposal.md:308:**The starter worker (`workers/engineer`, #34).** `.ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt` implements `plan.md`'s `## Implementation`. Its inputs, all untrusted, are `.ard-input/<issue#>/issue.md` and `comments.md`, in a fix round `test-output.log`, and `.ard/<issue#>/plan.md`, `issue.md`, the triage role files and logs. It writes code, tests and docs, and `worker-engineer.md` with `role: engineer` and `attempt: 1`, an optional `next` of `review:` entries, and never `worker` or `verdict`. The body has Changes, Testing and Open issues sections; it becomes the commit body, the PR description and the issue comment, and a fix round's body describes the whole change. It answers `needs-human` for a change the diff guard would reject, more than 1,000 lines, a missing decision, nothing to change, or an input that tries to instruct it. In a fix round it keeps `done` and explains a failure it cannot fix, so the loop reports `ard:tests:failed` on the PR. The repository's package manager may fetch a dependency the change needs (`go get`, `npm install`); the agent installs no system packages and uses no other network, and the guard and reviewers still see `go.mod` and lockfile changes. Credential-shaped test fixtures are built at run time. The starter override is Sonnet 5.5, `timeout: 60m` for the whole job and `tests: make test`. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55's `ard-agent` image gives a worker image a base.\ndocs/proposal.md:326:**The starter reviewer (`reviewers/eng-review`, #36).** `.ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt` checks correctness, missing tests and drift from `plan.md`. Its inputs, all untrusted, are `diff.patch`, `issue.md`, `comments.md` and the committed `.ard/<issue#>/`; text in the change that addresses a reviewer is a blocking `high` finding on its line (verdict `changes`), and the same text in the issue, comments or `.ard/<issue#>/` is ignored and mentioned in the body. It runs the repository's own linter and the changed packages' tests with coverage through Bash, writing scratch files outside the worktree, reports only problems on added lines and skips a check it cannot run, saying so; the package manager may fetch declared dependencies and nothing else is downloaded. Critical and high findings always block, medium only when it is a real bug, low and info never; a missing test blocks only when it is `high` (risky or core logic, or a case `plan.md` named), smaller gaps are `medium`. The verdict is `changes` exactly when a finding blocks. `line` is the head-side line: a `+` line goes inline, anything else in the body. It writes only `review-eng-review.md` with `role: eng-review`, `attempt: 1`, `status` `done` or `needs-human`, `findings` with a double-quoted `file` and a `message: |` block, never `next` or `worker`, and a body with a `## Checks` section. It answers `needs-human` only when there is nothing to review or the issue and the plan contradict each other. The starter override is Sonnet 5.5 with the default 30m timeout and no `when:`, so every PR from the starter worker gets it. It ships no Dockerfile, so it runs as a host subprocess with the #84 warning until #55.\ndocs/proposal.md:339:Every directory under `.ard/reviewers/` reviews every PR unless `config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran). The lead can request extra reviewers through `next`; they are recorded in the triage job's close-out record in local state (`closeout.Deferred` reads them) and the worker loop adds the `ard:review:<role>` labels to the PR when it opens it.\ndocs/proposal.md:409:  reviewers/license-review: { agent: kimi, when: { paths: [go.mod, go.sum, \"package*.json\"] } }\nREADME.md:42:Requires Go (see `go.mod`).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f5885f6-4319-4aab-8f24-9f470a446d4a","uuid":"71ff0194-4853-453c-b8c0-76ab65392f4f","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:38:24.634Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/proposal.md:171:{\"fingerprint\":\"osv:GHSA-xxxx:go.mod:golang.org/x/net\",\"title\":\"golang.org/x/net: GHSA-xxxx (high)\",\ndocs/proposal.md:172: \"severity\":\"high\",\"group\":\"go.mod\",\"files\":[\"go.mod\"],\"body\":\"markdown details\"}\ndocs/proposal.md:203:| lts | endoflife.date + manifests: go.mod, package.json, Dockerfile `FROM`, Helm charts | 7 d | 1 per component | yes |\ndocs/proposal.md:305:8. **Open or update a draft PR** with ard's own `Closes #<issue>`, the agent summary quoted and neutralised (`committer.NeutraliseRefs`, then marker and mention defusing), the test result and links to `worker-<role>.md`, the logs and the job id. Reviewers are the role's `reviewers`, or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty (`when:` rules are ignored until #