{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL7K8FQoDRMLA7otz8y3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VwheTvM83whmvupM3y13wu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"Reviewers are the role's `reviewers`, or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty (`when:` rules are ignored until #42), plus any `review:<role>` the lead deferred, limited to roles that exist, and requested only when the tests did not fail.\",\"Reviewers are chosen by `config.SelectReviewers`: the candidates are the role's `reviewers` (a list that only narrows), or every reviewer role when it is unset or empty, and each candidate's `when:` still decides. A `when:` matches when any path changed between the merge base of the config commit and the pushed head matches a `paths` entry, or a listed triage role ran (closed `done`, or its `ard:triage:<role>:done` label; `needs-human` does not count). Paths are case-sensitive and anchored at the repo root: `web/` is a directory, anything else a doublestar glob, so `**/go.mod` matches a root `go.mod` and `go.mod` only the root one; `.ard/` and `.ard-input/` paths are never selectable. Any `review:<role>` the lead deferred or the worker's own `next` lists is added regardless of `when:`, limited to roles that exist, and requested only when the tests did not fail. Selection is monotonic: each run recomputes from the whole PR diff and close-out only adds labels, so earlier requests stay and newly matching reviewers are added. When the head or git is unavailable, path rules fail open. If no reviewer is selected the PR stays a draft (the loop logs `worker.no_reviewers`).\")\ns=s.replace(\"unless `config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran). The lead\",\"unless `config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran; either is enough, and a `when:` with neither is an error). A worker's `reviewers:` list narrows the candidates but does not bypass `when:`. The lead\")\ns=s.replace(\"`config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran; either is enough, and a `when:` with neither is an error). A worker's `reviewers:` list narrows the candidates but does not bypass `when:`. The lead can request extra reviewers through `next`;\",\"`config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran; either is enough, and a `when:` with neither is an error). A worker's `reviewers:` list narrows the candidates but does not bypass `when:`. The lead (or the worker) can request extra reviewers through `next`, which bypasses `when:`;\")\ns=s.replace('when: { paths: [go.mod, go.sum, \"package*.json\"] } }','when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package*.json\"] } }\\n  reviewers/web-review: { when: { paths: [web/] } }')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 339p docs/proposal.md | head -c 900; grep -n \"web-review\" -B3 -A6 docs/proposal.md | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1981,"cache_read_input_tokens":65489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1981},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f5885f6-4319-4aab-8f24-9f470a446d4a","uuid":"12ef153b-2ced-4914-b66e-f9164edfe0c8","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:38:31.502Z","request_id":"req_011ChL7K86iyd6hZFbi9C2ps"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwheTvM83whmvupM3y13wu","type":"tool_result","content":"Every directory under `.ard/reviewers/` reviews every PR unless `config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran; either is enough, and a `when:` with neither is an error). A worker's `reviewers:` list narrows the candidates but does not bypass `when:`. The lead (or the worker) can request extra reviewers through `next`, which bypasses `when:`; they are recorded in the triage job's close-out record in local state (`closeout.Deferred` reads them) and the worker loop adds the `ard:review:<role>` labels to the PR when it opens it.\n407-  triage/engineer:          { after: [architect, product-manager, designer, documentation-planner] }\n408-  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout: 60m, reviewers: [security-review, eng-review] }\n409-  reviewers/license-review: { agent: kimi, when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package*.json\"] } }\n410:  reviewers/web-review: { when: { paths: [web/] } }\n411-```\n412-\n413-**Models are tiered (decided, #8).** Opus 5.5 for the lead, architect and security review; Sonnet 5.5 for workers, triage engineer and most reviewers; Haiku 5.5 for lint and docs work. The `budget_usd_per_day: 50` and per-job `max_budget_usd` values are provisional and are recalibrated from measured cost per job and per merged PR between Gate 1 and Gate 2.\n414-\n415-Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts and 3 review rounds. Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `:`, leading `-`, `..` or spaces; an abbreviated SHA is rejected, use all 40 characters); `ard config check` reports the file and key. A worker's `timeout` and `max_budget_usd` cover the whole job (every step), and `tests: \"\"` disables its test step. Per-role keys are `every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `timeout`, `agent`, `model`, `max_budget_usd`, `budget_usd_per_day`, `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `reviewers` and `when` (`paths`, or `triage` roles that ran). `plan_section` is for triage roles: the `## <heading>` of `plan.md` the role owns (one line, no leading `#`, unique across triage roles). The starter roles default to Requirements (product-manager), Design (architect), UX (designer), Docs (documentation-planner) and Implementation (engineer), and a value in `config.yaml` overrides that; a triage role with none may write only its own role file. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\n416-","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f5885f6-4319-4aab-8f24-9f470a446d4a","uuid":"1caa2469-15df-4118-b83c-92887e2a7229","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:38:31.544Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Every directory under `.ard/reviewers/` reviews every PR unless `config.yaml` gives it a `when:` rule (paths, or a triage role that ran; either is enough, and a `when:` with neither is an error). A worker's `reviewers:` list narrows the candidates but does not bypass `when:`. The lead (or the worker) can request extra reviewers through `next`, which bypasses `when:`; they are recorded in the triage job's close-out record in local state (`closeout.Deferred` reads them) and the worker loop adds the `ard:review:<role>` labels to the PR when it opens it.\n407-  triage/engineer:          { after: [architect, product-manager, designer, documentation-planner] }\n408-  workers/engineer:         { tests: make test, timeout